use @piton/belay
from ../Factory import Factory
from ./lib/FactorySkillBase import FactorySkillBase

export skill Factory0010Verify extends FactorySkillBase:
    description: Verify a factory implementation against the specification's conformance scenarios.
    useWhen: checking whether a factory implementation conforms, before adoption, or after a specification update
    prompt:
        Read @{Factory.conformanceScenarios}, @{Factory.verifierIdentity},
        @{Factory.reportAdmissibility}, @{Factory.conformanceReport},
        @{Factory.conformanceIndependence}, and @{Factory.conformanceVerdicts}.
        Confirm you are a distinct authenticated principal, not merely a new
        session, and that you are outside the recorded excluded set. Confirm
        you cannot modify the code under test and may only append one report.
        If independence cannot be established, stop and report that the
        verification is not admissible.

        Read the project descriptor and its recorded specification version.
        Map each claimed capability to its scenarios. Core scenarios are always
        required. Run each scenario with its stated setup, action, and expected
        observable. Record the invocation, observed value, evidence reference
        and hash, timestamps, and a verdict of pass, fail, unsupported, or
        not-applicable. A scenario that cannot be exercised is not silently
        passed.

        Store the report as a write-once evidence artifact and submit it for
        admission. Cite the base report for a delta re-run and cover every
        required scenario exactly once. A pass expires on any specification,
        implementation, descriptor, capability, or environment change, or after
        90 days.
        Report implementation gaps as failures. A claimed specification gap
        becomes an amendment proposal requiring engineer approval; it does not
        turn a failure into a pass.

        Do not repair the implementation during verification. Do not claim
        conformance from a report you cannot substantiate with evidence.
    result:
        Report the checklist and specification versions, the scenarios run and
        their verdicts, evidence locations, unsupported or not-applicable
        scenarios with reasons, and any amendment proposals.
